ubtract the area of the square from the area of the rectangle. Let me write that down: 18 square inches minus 25 square inches. Wait, that would be negative 7 square inches. But area can't be negative. Maybe I did something wrong here.\n\nHold on, let me check again. Maybe I got the dimensions mixed up. The rectangle's area is 3 times 6, which is 18. The square's side is 5, so 5 times 5 is 25. So, 25 minus 18 is 7. That difference is positive 7 square inches. Maybe the confusion was between length and width? Let me confirm.\n\nFor the rectangle, length is 3 and width is 6. So, yes, 3*6=18. For the square, since width is 5, then side length is 5, so 5*5=25. So the difference is indeed 7 square inches. Therefore, the answer should be 7. Maybe I made a sign error earlier, but since area is positive difference, it's 7.\n\nWait, but why does the answer come out as positive? Because the area of the square is larger than the rectangle. So, subtracting them gives 25 - 18 = 7. Yeah, that makes sense. I think that's correct. Let me just recap to make sure I didn't mix up any numbers.\n\nRectangle: length 3, width 6 → area = 3 * 6 = 18. Square: side 5 → area = 5 * 5 = 25. Difference between square and rectangle: 25 - 18 = 7. Yep, that seems right. So boxed answer would be \\boxed{7}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the difference in area between the given shapes, we begin by calculating the area of each shape:\n\n- **Area of the rectangle**:  \n  The length is $3$ inches and the width is $6$ inches. The area is calculated as:  \n  $$\n  \\text{Area} = \\text{length} \\times \\text{width} = 3 \\times 6 = 18 \\text{ square inches}\n  $$\n\n- **Area of the square**:  \n  The width of the square is $5$ inches, so the side length is also $5$ inches. The area is calculated as:  \n  $$\n  \\text{Area} = \\text{side} \\times \\text{side} = 5 \\times 5 = 25 \\text{ square inches}\n  $$\n\nNow, to find the difference in area:  \n$$\n25 - 18 = 7\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{7}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "A rectangle has a length of 3 inches and a width of 6 inches. A square has a width of 5 inches. What is the difference in area between the two shapes?", "answer": "The area of the rectangle is 3 x 6 = <<3*6=18>>18 sq in\nThe area of the square is 5 x 5 = <<5*5=25>>25 sq in\nThe difference is 25 - 18 = <<25-18=7>>7 sq in\n#### 7", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: A rectangle has a length of 3 inches and a width of 6 inches. A square has a width of 5 inches. What is the difference in area between the two shapes?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["7"], "solution": "7"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 362, 22756, 702, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 18, 14924, 323, 264, 2374, 315, 220, 21, 14924, 13, 362, 9334, 702, 264, 2374, 315, 220, 20, 14924, 13, 3555, 374, 279, 6672, 304, 3082, 1948, 279, 1378, 20816], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 419, 3491, 13, 2055, 11, 1052, 594, 264, 22756, 323, 264, 9334, 11, 323, 582, 1184, 311, 1477, 279, 6672, 304, 862, 5671, 13, 6771, 752, 1191, 553, 88646, 1128, 1817, 6083, 702, 382, 5338, 11, 279, 22756, 13, 576, 3491, 2727, 279, 3084, 374, 220, 18, 14924, 323, 279, 2374, 374, 220, 21]}
